Hi everyone, I'm Jordan MERRIFIELD, student at Sorbonne University (2026).

This sandbox is based on my 3-month M1 internship made with Mathilde Tavares and Francesco Picella.

During this internship, I studied diphasic flows and their interactions with embed boundaries. 

# Headers

I used Mathilde Tavares's header to impose the contact angle on the embed boundary [contact-embed](https://basilisk.fr/sandbox/tavares/contact-embed.h) and Théo Witkamp's header to compute the Navier boundary condition [embed_navier](https://basilisk.fr/sandbox/twitkamp/MovingEmbed/embed_navier.h).

I made my own header to follow properties of the interface : [interface_properties](https://basilisk.fr/sandbox/jmerrifield/interface_properties.h)

# Codes

## Capillary rise

My first test-case was the capillary rise. I used ([Aghar et al.,2024](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.camwa.2024.12.015)) as a reference.
I studied vertical capillary rise with [capillary_navier](https://basilisk.fr/sandbox/jmerrifield/Capillary/capillary_embed_navier.c) and without [capillary_noslip](https://basilisk.fr/sandbox/jmerrifield/Capillary/capillary_embed_noslip.c)  Navier slip condition as well as inclined capillary rise [capillary_inclined](https://basilisk.fr/sandbox/jmerrifield/Capillary/capillary_embed_inclined.c).


## Sessile spreading 

Following that, I studied the behaviour of spreading of a sessile on embed boundary. First, without gravity, to see the deformation due to capillary effects, and after with gravity to see its influence on the form of the sessile [sessile_grav](https://basilisk.fr/sandbox/jmerrifield/Sessile/sessile_embed_grav.c).